<mjml>
  <mj-head>
    <mj-font name="Montserrat" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Montserrat:wght@400;600;700&display=swap" />
    <mj-attributes>
      <mj-all font-family="Montserrat, Arial, sans-serif" />
      <mj-text font-size="15px" color="#333333" line-height="1.7" align="justify" />
    </mj-attributes>
    <mj-preview>How to build a Claude Dashboard on a Fabric semantic model. Plus a redesigned Theme Generator and our first data story.</mj-preview>
  </mj-head>
  <mj-body background-color="#f4f4f4" width="640px">

    <!-- Header banner -->
    <mj-section padding="0">
      <mj-column padding="0">
        <mj-image src="https://bibb.pro/images/newsletter/header.png" width="640px" padding="0" />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" padding="40px 40px 30px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text font-size="34px" font-weight="bold" color="#142328" line-height="1.2" align="center">
          Claude Dashboards on Power BI and Fabric. Plus a redesigned Theme Generator.
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Sponsor block — self-sponsored, Oscar's book -->
    <mj-section background-color="#e9f5f7" padding="24px 40px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" font-size="15px" color="#142328" padding-bottom="8px">
          This 19th edition of the bibb newsletter is brought to you by:
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text align="center" font-size="16px" font-weight="bold" color="#142328" padding-bottom="12px">
          Power Query for Excel and Business Users
        </mj-text>
        <mj-image src="https://bibb.pro/images/book/power-query-cover.jpg" href="https://bibb.pro/book/power-query/" width="200px" padding-bottom="12px" border-radius="6px" />
        <mj-text align="center" font-size="14px" color="#142328" padding-top="4px">
          My book for the finance analyst, the operations lead and everyone who cleans the same Excel data every Monday by hand. Build it once in Power Query, refresh it forever. No programming background needed.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-button href="https://bibb.pro/book/power-query/" align="center" background-color="#FF0020" color="#ffffff" width="200px">
          Get the book
        </mj-button>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Oscar's Take -->
    <mj-section background-color="#f9f9f9" padding="30px 40px 8px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text font-size="11px" font-weight="bold" color="#FF0020" letter-spacing="2px" padding-bottom="12px">
          OSCAR'S TAKE
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          <table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" role="presentation">
            <tr>
              <td style="padding-right:14px;vertical-align:middle;">
                <img src="https://bibb.pro/images/authors/oscar-martinez.png" width="56" height="56" style="border-radius:50%;display:block;" alt="Oscar" />
              </td>
              <td style="vertical-align:middle;">
                <div style="font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;color:#142328;line-height:1.4;">Oscar Martinez</div>
                <div style="font-size:13px;color:#888888;line-height:1.4;">Editor, bibb Newsletter</div>
              </td>
            </tr>
          </table>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <mj-section background-color="#f9f9f9" padding="0 40px 30px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text>
          The last edition went out in August, the week <a href="https://bibb.pro/book/power-query/" style="color:#FF0020;">my book</a> launched. Then this inbox went quiet for twelve weeks. A new role and a master's semester will do that. The site did not stop, though, and I owe you the catch-up.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          First, a very hot topic: Claude Dashboards came out on October 8, and I dropped everything to point it at a Fabric semantic model. Three days later <a href="https://bibb.pro/post/claude-dashboards-microsoft-fabric-iq-mcp/" style="color:#FF0020;">the guide</a> was live. It works, through the <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/fabric/iq/connectors/fabric-iq-mcp" style="color:#FF0020;">Fabric IQ MCP server</a>, but it is a snapshot, not a live feed. Several routes failed before one worked, and the guide covers that route, the setup, and the quirks we hit.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          Second, the <a href="https://bibb.pro/apps/theme-generator/" style="color:#FF0020;">Theme Generator</a> got a major redesign. Same features, same ease of use you already know. What changed is the workspace around them. It is cleaner, and it gives us room to grow, so the next features have a place to land without making the simple path harder.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          We also tried a new format: data stories. The first one is about <a href="https://bibb.pro/post/understanding-the-grain/" style="color:#FF0020;">the grain</a>, the decision you make before you write a single query. A story you scroll through lets you see what your data forgets each time you aggregate it. All three are below, plus a few <a href="https://bibb.pro/blog/" style="color:#FF0020;">posts</a> you may have missed. If one is useful, hit reply and tell me which.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-social font-size="12px" icon-size="22px" mode="horizontal" align="left" padding-top="8px" padding-bottom="0">
          <mj-social-element src="https://www.mailjet.com/images/theme/v1/icons/ico-social/linkedin.png" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/oscarmartinezv/" background-color="#0077b5" padding="4px" />
          <mj-social-element name="youtube" href="https://www.youtube.com/@bibb_pro" background-color="#FF0020" padding="4px" />
        </mj-social>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Divider -->
    <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" padding="0 40px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-divider border-color="#e0e0e0" border-width="1px" padding="0" />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Lead card — Claude Dashboards on Fabric -->
    <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" padding="24px 40px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-image src="https://bibb.pro/images/blog/heros/claude-dashboards-microsoft-fabric-iq-mcp.png" href="https://bibb.pro/post/claude-dashboards-microsoft-fabric-iq-mcp/" border-radius="6px" padding-bottom="16px" />
        <mj-text font-size="18px" font-weight="bold" color="#142328" line-height="1.3" padding-bottom="8px">
          Building Claude Dashboards on Microsoft Fabric with Fabric IQ MCP
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text font-size="14px" color="#555555">
          How to connect Claude to a Fabric semantic model step by step: the tenant setting, the Azure app registration, and the two MCP connectors. Then Claude runs DAX against your model, saves the results as CSV snapshots and builds the dashboard on top. Includes the connector quirks we hit and why the result is a snapshot, not live data.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-button href="https://bibb.pro/post/claude-dashboards-microsoft-fabric-iq-mcp/" align="left" padding-top="10px" padding-bottom="6px" background-color="#FF0020">
          Read the guide
        </mj-button>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Divider -->
    <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" padding="0 40px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-divider border-color="#e0e0e0" border-width="1px" padding="0" />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Feature card — Theme Generator -->
    <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" padding="24px 40px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-image src="https://bibb.pro/images/blog/heros/power-bi-json-report-theme-generator-by-bibb.png" href="https://bibb.pro/apps/theme-generator/" border-radius="6px" padding-bottom="16px" />
        <mj-text font-size="18px" font-weight="bold" color="#142328" line-height="1.3" padding-bottom="8px">
          The Theme Generator, redesigned
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text font-size="14px" color="#555555">
          A new workspace, the same tool you know. Start from a palette, a Coolors link, an image or a short prompt, preview the theme on a sample dashboard or your own Power BI report, and download a valid JSON in HD or Full HD (beta). B.I.ST is still there when you want to edit the full JSON.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-button href="https://bibb.pro/apps/theme-generator/" align="left" padding-top="10px" padding-bottom="6px" background-color="#FF0020">
          Open the Theme Generator
        </mj-button>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Divider -->
    <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" padding="0 40px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-divider border-color="#e0e0e0" border-width="1px" padding="0" />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Feature card — The Grain (first data story, no hero image) -->
    <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" padding="24px 40px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text font-size="11px" font-weight="bold" color="#FF0020" letter-spacing="2px" padding-bottom="8px">
          NEW FORMAT: DATA STORY
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text font-size="18px" font-weight="bold" color="#142328" line-height="1.3" padding-bottom="8px">
          Understanding the Grain
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text font-size="14px" color="#555555">
          Follow one record out of 72 as you scroll. Group by color, then by shape, then into a single total, and watch what each aggregation keeps and what it forgets. The point: aggregation is not the mistake. Accidental aggregation is.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-button href="https://bibb.pro/post/understanding-the-grain/" align="left" padding-top="10px" padding-bottom="6px" background-color="#FF0020">
          View the story
        </mj-button>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Divider -->
    <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" padding="0 40px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-divider border-color="#e0e0e0" border-width="1px" padding="0" />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Since the last edition -->
    <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" padding="24px 40px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text font-size="11px" font-weight="bold" color="#FF0020" letter-spacing="2px" padding-bottom="12px">
          SINCE THE LAST EDITION
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text font-size="14px" color="#555555" padding-bottom="10px">
          <a href="https://bibb.pro/post/power-bi-svg-measures/" style="color:#FF0020;font-weight:bold;">Power BI SVG Measures: 7 Use Cases, 17 Rules, and an AI Prompt</a><br />
          Sajjad Ahmadi on where SVG measures earn their place, the rules that stop them breaking, and a prompt template to generate them.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text font-size="14px" color="#555555" padding-bottom="10px">
          <a href="https://bibb.pro/post/connect-clockify-to-power-bi/" style="color:#FF0020;font-weight:bold;">Connecting Clockify to Power BI: Three Integration Patterns That Work</a><br />
          Hand-written API calls, the free custom connector, or a ready template. Pick by build versus ship.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text font-size="14px" color="#555555" padding-bottom="10px">
          <a href="https://bibb.pro/post/bibb-analytics-introduction/" style="color:#FF0020;font-weight:bold;">bibb Analytics: Build in Public</a><br />
          We had GA4 running since day one and no strategy behind it. This series fixes that in the open, starting with the <a href="https://bibb.pro/post/bibb-analytics-introduction/" style="color:#FF0020;">introduction</a> and the <a href="https://bibb.pro/post/bibb-analytics-strategy/" style="color:#FF0020;">measurement strategy</a>.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text font-size="14px" color="#555555">
          <span style="color:#142328;font-weight:bold;">Also new:</span> the <a href="https://bibb.pro/apps/theme-generator-style-icons/" style="color:#FF0020;">Style Icon Presets</a> app, and many more ready-made icons in the <a href="https://bibb.pro/apps/theme-generator-cf-icons/" style="color:#FF0020;">Conditional Formatting Icons</a> app.
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" padding="24px 40px 16px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-social font-size="12px" icon-size="22px" mode="horizontal" align="left" padding-bottom="10px">
          <mj-social-element src="https://www.mailjet.com/images/theme/v1/icons/ico-social/linkedin.png" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/bibb" background-color="#0077b5" />
        </mj-social>
        <mj-text font-size="11px" color="#aaaaaa" line-height="1.6">
          © 2026 bibb<br />
          This e-mail has been sent to [[EMAIL_TO]], <a href="[[UNSUB_LINK_EN]]" style="color:#aaaaaa;text-decoration:none;">click here to unsubscribe</a>.
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

  </mj-body>
</mjml>
